 Boebert (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Lauren Boebert seeks reelection in a Colorado district that leans Republican by about nine points, facing Democrat Eileen Laubacher and a Libertarian candidate. Expert raters mostly place the race in Likely or Solid Republican territory, though three outlets call it a Tossup, and prediction markets give Boebert roughly a two-in-three chance. No general-election polls are available, so the picture rests on fundamentals and ratings.\n\nThe most striking dynamic is money: Laubacher has raised about $10.3 million and holds $3.6 million on hand, while Boebert has raised about $1.0 million with just $247,000 banked. That gap gives the challenger resources to define the race, but the district's partisan lean and incumbency remain strong counters. The forecast lands on a Republican edge of several points, with meaningful uncertainty given the absence of polling.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.1824, "margin": -5.77}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.3343, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.1945, "margin": -6.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.2743, "margin": -4.7}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.2626, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.23, "margin": -4.7}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.2582, "margin": -4.8}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.2829, "margin": -4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.2916, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.2767, "margin": -4.5}]}